          "title": "Time first, verb second",
          "body": "In a German statement, the verb always comes **second**. You can start with a time instead of *ich*, but then the subject moves **after** the verb:\n\n- *Ich arbeite morgen.*\n- ***Morgen** arbeite ich.*\n\nBoth mean *I'm working tomorrow*. Starting with the time is very common.",
